## R-transparency proof, check 2: the front square alone, fully opaque --
## the reference front_opaque value check 2's arithmetic scales by Opacity
## to predict front_alone. Not third-party.
Display "transparency_front_opaque.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [40]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.1]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [1.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [5 0 -5] "to" [0 0 0]
Sides 2
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.1] "Kd" [0.9]

AttributeBegin
	Translate 0 0 -2
	Color [0.8 0.2 0.2]
	Opacity [1 1 1]
	Polygon "P" [-0.4 -0.4 0  0.4 -0.4 0  0.4 0.4 0  -0.4 0.4 0]
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
